P(f"The final labels add a governance view (Figure 7 in Results). Agency and action control (D1) and input trust and goal integrity (D4) dominate and appear together in {pd.read_csv(T / 'rq1_cooccurrence.csv', index_col=0).loc['D1','D4']} cases: untrusted content leads an agent to run a command. Transparency (D3) and accountability (D7) are rare. The GCS is concentrated between 50% and 60% (median 57.1%) and is left-skewed (skewness = −2.35), because most cases breach two to four of five to ten applicable controls. One more EDA finding mattered for RQ3: the share of high-impact cases rises from 41% among single-domain cases to 78% among two-domain cases and to 85% or more among cases with four or more domains. This motivated keeping the number of domains as a covariate.")
