H2("Minimum Sample Size")
P("Each research question has its own sample-size calculation matched to its analysis, all with α = .05 (two-sided) and power = .80 (Table 4). RQ1 estimates a proportion, so the confidence-interval method with the most conservative p = .50 and a margin of ±.07 is used. RQ2 tests association in a 4 × 2 table (df = 3), so the noncentral chi-square power method is used with Cohen's (1988) effect size w = 0.25, between small and medium. RQ3 tests a continuous predictor in logistic regression, so the method of Hsieh et al. (1998) is used with the observed high-impact proportion P = .70 and a target OR of 0.61 per standard deviation (SD), inflated for the variance the covariates share with GCS (R² = .20). RQ4 estimates an agreement proportion with the confidence-interval method, using expected accuracy a = .80 (Zheng et al., 2023) and a margin of ±.06.")
